1. Super Agent Overview

Super Agent is Genspark's flagship feature, launched in April 2025, a no-code autonomous agent. Users describe a goal in one natural-language sentence; Super Agent plans tasks, chooses tools, and generates deliverables automatically.

1.1 Underlying Architecture

- Coordinates 9 specialized large language models (later expanded to 30+)
- Integrates 80+ built-in tools (later expanded to 150+)
- Uses GPT-4.1 for research and structured output (1M-token context)
- Uses GPT-image-1 for image generation
- Uses OpenAI Realtime API for real-time voice (Call For Me)
- Asynchronous cloud processing: tasks continue while users are offline

1.2 Core Value Proposition

"One prompt = one deliverable (or action)" — Super Agent moves users from typing in a conversation to receiving a finished result.

2. Follow Up (Follow-Up Questions)

2.1 Post-Response Follow-up Suggestions

After every response, Genspark automatically shows follow-up buttons underneath (typically 3-4), each a complete clickable prompt. This Follow-up Suggestions pattern shifts conversation from user-led to system guidance + user choice, substantially increasing session depth and feature adoption.

2.2 Follow-Up Generation Prompt Design (Reverse-Engineered with Claude)

This is the heart of the feature. A high-quality follow-up prompt usually includes:

Role definition  "You are a conversation planner helping users explore topics in depth"
Input context  Combine the user's original question + full AI response as model context
Count constraint  "Generate exactly 4 follow-up questions, no more and no fewer"
Diversity requirement  "The 4 questions should cover different directions: deeper details, comparisons, format transformation, practical application" — essential to avoiding repetitive questions
Format constraint  "Each follow-up is a complete, directly sendable Chinese question, beginning with the Chinese word for 'please,' 15-40 characters"
Prohibitions  "Do not repeat what the user already asked; stay within the current topic"
Structured-output Schema  Enforce `{ followups: string[4] }` through JSON Schema for reliable frontend parsing
